      "seed": 1797300766,
      "version": 2372,
      "versionNonce": 1788028894,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788856087400,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is abstract method \n======================\n\n1. Abstract method is a method in an abstract class or\ninterface for which we do not provide any\nbody/implementation.\n\n\n2. to make any method abstract we prefix it with\n'abstract' keyword .\n\n synatax\n==========\n\npublic abstract <return_type> <method_name> ( );\n\nor \n\nabstract public <return_type> <method_name> ( );\n\n\nRules for abstarct methods\n=========================\n\n1. abstract methods can only be declared in abstract\nclass, that is class must also be declared as abstract .\n\n2. That is abstarct methods can live inside abstract\nclass only , but abstarct class can have non abstract\nmethods also .\n\n3. If a class is abstract than we are not allowed to\ncreate its object but we can create its reference.\n\n4.Because if it were allowed, there would be no\nimplementation available for an abstract method to\nexecute.\n\n5. An abstract class reference can refer to a child class\nobject and can access the members available through the\nabstract class reference.\n\n6. If a class is abstract there are two impulsion \n\n   a. child class must override every abstarct method of\nparent class .\n\n   b. Otherwise child class must also be declared as\nabstract .\n\n7. Abstarct class can contain everything a concrete class\ncan have .\n\n Can every type of methods can be declared as abstract .\n\n--> No four types methods cannot be declared as static \n\n1. constructor - Because abstarction is used in\ninheritance and constructor cannot be inherited thus\ncannot be overriden .\n\n2. static method - Because static method follow early\nbinding and due to early binding java would allways run\nparent method but parent method doesn't have body and\nthus java would be confused therefore static methods\nare not allowed to be declared as abstract .\n\n3. private - because private methods cannot be inherited .\n\n4. final \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is abstract method \n======================\n\n1. Abstract method is a method in an abstract class or interface for which we do not provide any body/implementation.\n\n\n2. to make any method abstract we prefix it with 'abstract' keyword .\n\n synatax\n==========\n\npublic abstract <return_type> <method_name> ( );\n\nor \n\nabstract public <return_type> <method_name> ( );\n\n\nRules for abstarct methods\n=========================\n\n1. abstract methods can only be declared in abstract class, that is class must also be declared as abstract .\n\n2. That is abstarct methods can live inside abstract class only , but abstarct class can have non abstract methods also .\n\n3. If a class is abstract than we are not allowed to create its object but we can create its reference.\n\n4.Because if it were allowed, there would be no implementation available for an abstract method to execute.\n\n5. An abstract class reference can refer to a child class object and can access the members available through the abstract class reference.\n\n6. If a class is abstract there are two impulsion \n\n   a. child class must override every abstarct method of parent class .\n\n   b. Otherwise child class must also be declared as abstract .\n\n7. Abstarct class can contain everything a concrete class can have .\n\n Can every type of methods can be declared as abstract .\n\n--> No four types methods cannot be declared as static \n\n1. constructor - Because abstarction is used in inheritance and constructor cannot be inherited thus cannot be overriden .\n\n2. static method - Because static method follow early binding and due to early binding java would allways run parent method but parent method doesn't have body and thus java would be confused therefore static methods are not allowed to be declared as abstract .\n\n3. private - because private methods cannot be inherited .\n\n4. final \n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
